.superpowers/
.venv/
__pycache__/
# `uv pip install -e .` — the setup command since claude-console became a
# declared dependency — leaves this behind. Machine-specific build output.
*.egg-info/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Parallel-feature worktrees (each is an isolated checkout; never tracked).
# They live INSIDE the repo on purpose. A worktree parked in a sibling folder
# is easy to lose track of, and the cost is not theoretical: three features
# were built in `../task_tracker-worktrees/` on 2026-07-25, the primary
# checkout drifted onto a feature branch, and the app was launched for an hour
# from a tree that did not contain the code being tested. Keeping them here
# means one `git worktree list` from the repo root shows every checkout, and
# this rule is what stops a nested checkout showing up as untracked junk in
# the parent's `git status`.
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/

# Design specs, implementation plans, prototypes and per-feature intent notes.
# Kept on disk — they are the record of why things are the way they are, and one
# of them is the reproduction asset for an open bug — but not published. This is
# a public repo, and that material is working notes rather than documentation:
# it quotes conversations, names other projects on this machine, and carries
# absolute paths into a home directory. CLAUDE.md and .claude/rules/ are the
# current documentation; those are tracked, and they are what a reader needs.
docs/superpowers/
.planning/

# Iteration round ledgers and their lineage chains. Same reasoning, and more so:
# these files exist to hold his words VERBATIM, plus what was rejected and why.
# That is the whole value and it is also exactly what should not be published.
# Listed here rather than left merely untracked, because untracked survives only
# until someone stages a directory.
.iteration/

# This machine's own paths — the claude-console checkout the setup command wants.
# Personal, per-checkout, and the reason pyproject.toml no longer names one.
CLAUDE.local.md
